_meanings:
.²1 As a prefix to verbs it means ‘forward’, ‘forth’, ‘in front’, ‘onward’,
 ‘before’, ‘away’, as in {#pragam, prasTA, pracar, prayA#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 With adjectives it means ‘very’, ‘excessively’, ‘very much’ <ab>&c.</ab>; {#prakfzwa#},
 {#pramatta#} <ab>&c.</ab>, see further on.
.²3 With nouns whether derived from verbs or not, it is used in the following
 senses according to <ls>G. M.</ls>:--
.³({%a%}) beginning, commencement; ({#prayARam, prasTAnam, prAhRa#});
.³({%b%}) length ({#prabAlaBUzika#});
.³({%c%}) power ({#praBu#});
.³({%d%}) intensity, excess ({#pravAda, prakarza, pracCAya praguRa#});
.³({%e%}) source or origin ({#praBava, prapOtra#});
.³({%f%}) completion, perfectness, satisfaction ({#praBuktamannam#});
.³({%g%}) destitution, separation, being without ({#prozitA, praparRavfkzaH#});
.³({%h%}) apart ({#prajYu#});
.³({%i%}) excellence ({#prAcAryaH#});
.³({%j%}) purity ({#prasannaM jalam#});
.³({%k%}) wish ({#prArTanA#});
.³({%l%}) cessation ({#praSama#});
.³({%m%}) adoration, respect ({#prAYjaliH#} who respectfully folds his
 hands together);
.³({%n%}) prominence ({#praRasa, pravAla#}). In the Veda it is often used
 as a separable adverb; <ab>cf.</ab> {#pra AdikarmadIrGeSaBfSasaMBavatfptiviyogaSudDiSaktIcCASAntipUjAgradarSanezu#}.
